SUMMARY:IT Gr 12 T1 W1: Pascal 24 SQLite databases in Delphi (or lesson 25\
 , in Lazarus) | What makes a computer fast
DESCRIPTION:CAPS Grade 12 - Pascal - Other three-term independent school (I
 SASA guideline) - T1 W1\n\nProgramming:\n- Pascal 24 (part): SQLite databas
 es in Delphi (or lesson 25\, in Lazarus)\n    focus: SQL from a program\, i
 ncluding queries with a parameter from the user\n    https://itcoder.co.za/
 lesson.php?c=pascal&id=capssqlitedelphi\n- Pascal 105 (part): The Grade 12 
 PAT - CAPS\n    focus: starting the PAT: task description and analysis of r
 equirements\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=pascal&id=capspat12\n\n
 Theory:\n- What makes a computer fast\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php
 ?c=theory12&id=performance\n\nDatabases:\n- SQL 1 (part): Good data in a da
 tabase\n    focus: caring for data: validation\, verification\, integrity\n
     https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdata\n- SQL 4: A good desig
 n\n    focus: a good database: integrity\, redundancy\; anomalies\, and rem
 oving them (the concept of normalisation): split tables and create relation
 s\n    https://itcoder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbdesign\n- SQL 5: Normali
 sation step by step\n    focus: anomalies\, and removing them - the concept
  of normalisation (the formal normal forms go beyond CAPS)\n    https://itc
 oder.co.za/lesson.php?c=sql&id=dbnormal
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
